<p>On the basis of exchange rates from 11-14 April, the UK's RMG is greater than +5 per cent at 5.599. It is therefore, currently forecast to enter the first of a possible five confirmation periods on 21 April, prior to a possible revaluation on 11 June 1997. All other green rates are currently forecast to remain unchanged. The largest 3-day bilateral gap (5.764 per cent) is that between the RMGs of the UK and Austria. If this were to exceed 6 per cent, the 3-day rule would be triggered. This would commence the confirmation period before 21 April and could lead to a possible UK green rate revaluation as early as 5 June 1997.</p>
